<title>UK: EIB adds 50 mln marks to 10-year structured bond.</title>
<headline>EIB adds 50 mln marks to 10-year structured bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to 200 million marks from 150 million marks, lead manager Morgan Stanley said on Thursday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT   *200 MLN DEM   COUPON   **8.0	 MATURITY    14.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE   FIX/REV FRN   ISS PRICE  101.875   PAY DATE ***14.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0	 REC REOFF  100.25    SPREAD	=</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX/FFT   PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.375     SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES     *ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED 24.JAN.97 AND INCREASED</p>
<p>		28.JAN.97</p>
<p>	    **YEARS ONE TO FOUR, THEN 16.0 PCT LESS TWO TIMES</p>
<p>		SIX-MONTH LIBOR</p>
<p>	   ***PLUS ACCRUED INTEREST</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
